Each check has a chance of finding a trap, which is about 1/3 at the
beginning of the game. So check multiple times, if you don't want to
get the trap effects. Once you've detected a trap, the chance of
successfully disarming it is dependent on dexterity, XL, and DL. Since
trap effects can be quite nasty, caution is advised; you might choose
not to try to disarm the trap (you won't set it off just by
searching), and instead leave the box or chest for later, when you are
more dextrous and experienced (and, ideally, have poison and fire
resistance).


